  "final_text": "I fixed the bug in `activity/timeparse.py`. The 12-hour time parser read \"12:xx AM\" as hour 12 (noon) instead of hour 0 (midnight). So \"2026-03-02 12:10 AM\" came out as midday on March 2, which created a fake 12-hour gap and split the overnight session in two.\n\n`parse_12h` now converts 12 AM to hour 0, the same way it already handled PM times. With that change the midnight test gives 1 session averaging 40 minutes, and all 7 tests pass. I didn't touch any test files and didn't commit anything."
